# JavaScript / React Rules

- Match the existing package manager, module system, lint rules, and component patterns.
- Do not introduce TypeScript unless explicitly approved; the project requirement is JavaScript.
- Validate user input at boundaries and handle async errors explicitly.
- Keep components focused and accessible. Include loading, empty, success, and error states where relevant.
- Avoid adding dependencies unless the benefit is explained.
- Add tests for user-visible behavior and important edge cases.
